            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 67-year-old male, admitted on 06/02/2000 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia. Spirometry confirmed severe airflow obstruction. During his stay, the patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored continuously. The patient was discharged in stable condition on 07/02/2000 with adjusted outpatient medication. Please ensure follow-up spirometry and ongoing COPD monitoring. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
